cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use mcp-recon in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  below. Findings emitted against specific MCP servers should additionally
  cite the upstream server they were discovered against.
title: mcp-recon
abstract: >-
  A reconnaissance and classification tool for the Model Context Protocol
  (MCP) ecosystem. Enumerates tool surfaces, fuzzes them with schema-aware
  adversarial inputs, classifies tools by reviewer-relevant risk
  (privileged, confused-deputy, etc.), and emits capability caveats that
  downstream issuers (e.g. capnagent) accept. Companion to capnagent on
  the defensive side.
type: software
